WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.568
-Thank you so much
for being here, buddy.

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:03.903
It's the first time
I'm introducing you as a dad.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.005
-As a father, yeah.
-You're a father.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.405
Congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:08.941
That's the best news!
-Thank you. Yeah, it's huge.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.243
It's pretty excellent.

00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:13.513
-Is your phone just all pictures
of kids now?

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.049
-Oh, for good reason I don't
have it on me right now.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.517
-Or else you'd show it?

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.052
-Or else I would absolutely
show it to you

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.720
'cause I am 100% that dad.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.223
-Yeah, I think there are
whole server farms

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.824
dedicated to just pictures
of my baby now.

00:00:25.824 --> 00:00:28.360
Like tens of --
it's amazing how many pictures

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.729
you can take of one baby.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.731
-Yeah, what -- Was it always
like sunsets and brunches?

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:34.300
-Or, yeah --
-Breakfast?

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.303
-She gets pasta sauce on her
face, we need 10,000 of those.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.604
-Oh, no.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.273
-Are you showing it to strangers
and everybody like you --

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.174
-Checked into the hotel
last night.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:45.077
First thing I did was like,
"Hey, did you know I had a baby?

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.779
[ Laughter ]
Have you seen my baby?

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.314
She's super cute."

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.716
And I know all parents think
their kids are super cute,

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:53.686
but my kid is, like,
really super cute.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.587
-Your wife is
Jodie Turner-Smith,

00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:57.791
a very talented actor.

00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:00.359
So please, give her my best.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.294
I saw this online
that made me laugh.

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:05.731
This is your wife rocking
a Pacey T-shirt.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:06.866
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.935
No, this popped up like

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.903
eight or nine months
into our relationship.

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:14.140
I'm not exactly sure
who the Amazon seller is

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.008
that keeps the Pacey shirts
on hand,

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:18.611
but she is their core customer.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.846
-Did you guys always know that
you were destined --

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.816
that you were going to
get married?

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.583
-I knew the moment she asked me.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.786
[ Laughter ]
-She asked you?

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.887
-She asked me, yeah,
on New Year's Eve.

00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:30.256
We were in Nicaragua.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.658
It was very beautiful,
incredibly romantic.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:35.461
We're walking down the beach,
and she asked me to marry her.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:38.197
-She just said will you -- Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.033
-No, there was,
like, a preamble.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.267
There was a lead-up to it.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.602
Did you know that
it was going to happen?

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:45.004
-I did not know,
but she was quite adamant,

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.072
and she was right.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.574
This is the best choice
I ever made.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.074
-Aw, that's what I'm
talking about, buddy.

00:01:49.074 --> 00:01:51.144
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, that's awesome.

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.078
Congrats on the great reviews.
-Thank you.

00:01:53.078 --> 00:01:55.314
-"Dr. Death" --
It's streaming now on Peacock.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:56.782
Everyone, get Peacock.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.684
By the way, super easy
to get Peacock.

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:02.788
-And a little bonus news --
You don't actually have to pay.

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.157
You should, of course.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.492
But you can watch the show
just by downloading the app.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:07.927
-Yeah, so it's free.
-It's free.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.862
-Yeah, so just do it.
-Love that.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.631
-Free is good.
-Free is great.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.999
-I tied it, 'cause I'm like,
"I should. It's NBC Peacock."

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:15.667
-I mean, you kind of got to.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.036
So I jumped in to it.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.938
I know, but I jumped in
to see how hard it was.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.106
It's easy.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.273
-It's fantastic.
-Super simple.

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:22.575
-Yeah.
-No excuses.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.843
-No.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:27.680
But this is based on
a troubling true story.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.615
-Yes.
-Craziness.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:32.018
Is this -- How did you find out
about the story?

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:35.555
-I missed -- So, this is
based on a true story.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.257
This terrible doctor,
Christopher Duntsch,

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:42.094
had 38 surgeries,
33 of which were catastrophic,

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.163
2 of which ended in death.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.032
A third one of his patients
has since died.

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:49.601
Just could not be any worse.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.170
-I missed all of this
while it was happening.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.138
So when the job came to me,
Patrick Macmanus,

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:56.008
who is the executive producer
and the writer, he --

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:57.977
we're talking on the phone and
he's giving me the whole pitch.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.546
And he basically said, "Look,
there's an amazing podcast.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.948
Go listen to the podcast and
then let's talk about it again."

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:04.583
So I went and listened to
the podcast.

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:07.286
And it -- I mean, it's like
a horror story.

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.588
You know, you cannot believe --

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:09.622
-It's even worse
than a horror story.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.190
-Yeah, it is 'cause it's true,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.025
and real bodies were damaged.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:16.529
And this man is probably going
to spend the rest of his life

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.930
in jail, as he well should.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.799
But the system that created him
still exists.

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:23.102
And that's, to me, what's so
scary about this story,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:27.406
is that he's the kind of
perfect storm of evil man

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:31.443
with bad intentions, but it took
a whole system around him

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.879
to allow him to keep on doing
that damage to people

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.914
and that system still exists.

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:37.650
-Gosh. You're phenomenal.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.286
Also it's Alec Baldwin
and Christian Slater too.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.788
-AnnaSophia Robb -- We got
a bunch of good folks in there.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:43.989
-Watch the show.
You're going to love it.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:45.091
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.059
Here's Joshua Jackson
in "Dr. Death."

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.694
Take a look at this.

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:51.731
-What happened with Mr. Peduo?

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:55.801
-Well, the surgery was normal,
nothing out of the ordinary.

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:58.504
With the exception
of a scrub tech

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.439
who had the pace of molasses
and a resident --

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:03.476
-It says here the procedure
was delayed.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.245
For a week.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.579
-Yes.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.114
There were some challenges
with the scheduling,

00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:10.516
but we accommodated.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.285
-Challenges?

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.888
-The access surgeons,
they were all booked up.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:19.058
-I was a nurse for many years
before entering management.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.093
I'm so fluent
in doctor bull[bleep]

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.929
I can whiff it all the way
from Fort Worth.

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.265
-Hey, look, I'm not trying to
cause trouble here,

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:31.103
but I think there are some
fragile male egos in this town

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:33.339
that don't like my style.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.308
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.410
-Joshua Jackson, everybody!

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.246
"Dr. Death" is streaming
now on Peacock!

